# Go API Standards

- Use stdlib `net/http`; no framework (Echo, Gin, etc.)
- All DB access via `internal/db/` with pgx
- Return JSON with appropriate status codes; use `api.WriteJSON` / `api.WriteError` helpers
- Admin endpoints: check Bearer token via `api.RequireAdmin` middleware
- Cron triggers: optionally validate `X-Cron-Secret` when `CRON_SECRET` is set
- Add new endpoints in `main.go` or `internal/api/`; keep route registration centralized
- Use `context.Context` for timeouts and cancellation in handlers that call external services
- **Sentry:** When `SENTRY_DSN` is set, significant errors must reach Sentry—not only `log.Printf`. HTTP: `sentryhttp` wraps the mux; if you handle an error and return 5xx without a panic, call `sentry.CaptureException`. Background jobs / goroutines: use `internal/sentryutil` with tags. See [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](../../docs/ARCHITECTURE.md#error-monitoring-sentry).
